Three gaps:

**1. 120-char line length** — `rustfmt` is correctly set to 120 (`max_width = 120` in `.rustfmt.toml`). Clippy doesn't enforce line length; that's rustfmt's job. ✅ for formatting, nothing to add.

**2. Rust lint rules** — `.clippy.toml` has only MSRV + argument/line-count thresholds. No pedantic/nursery/best-practices lints. We have `#![deny(clippy::all)]` in `packages/michi-node/src/lib.rs` but nothing in the main lib. Recommend adding to `src/lib.rs`:

```rust
#![warn(clippy::pedantic)]
#![warn(clippy::nursery)]
#![warn(clippy::cargo)]
#![allow(clippy::module_name_repetitions)]  // common false positive
```

`pedantic`/`nursery` will likely surface warnings we'd need to triage and either fix or explicitly allow.

**3. TS/JS linting** — Nothing. `packages/michi-node/package.json` only has `@napi-rs/cli`. The only JS source is `__test__/index.test.mjs` (the generated `index.js`/`index.d.ts` shouldn't be linted). oxlint would be the right choice — fast, minimal config, no TypeScript compiler needed.

Want me to add all three? I'd suggest running the pedantic/nursery pass first so we see what warnings come up before deciding what to allow vs fix. And for oxlint, it would just go in `package.json` as a devDep with a `lint` script.

Here are the findings. Solid research — actionable and opinionated. Here's what I'd recommend implementing:

---

### A. `src/lib.rs` — crate-level lint attributes

```rust
// rustc
#![warn(missing_docs)]
#![warn(unreachable_pub)]
#![warn(unused_qualifications)]
#![warn(unused_lifetimes)]

// clippy groups
#![warn(clippy::all)]
#![warn(clippy::pedantic)]
#![allow(clippy::module_name_repetitions)]  // ToonOptions, render_toon etc. — idiomatic
#![allow(clippy::must_use_candidate)]       // rendering fns return String, callers choose
#![allow(clippy::missing_errors_doc)]       // re-evaluate once # Errors sections are added

// clippy::restriction — safety (matches existing CLAUDE.md non-negotiables)
#![warn(clippy::unwrap_used)]
#![warn(clippy::expect_used)]
#![warn(clippy::panic)]
#![warn(clippy::todo)]
#![warn(clippy::unimplemented)]
#![warn(clippy::indexing_slicing)]
#![warn(clippy::disallowed_macros)]        // blocks println!/eprintln!/dbg! in lib code

// performance (string rendering crate — this matters)
#![warn(clippy::string_to_string)]
#![warn(clippy::inefficient_to_string)]

// style
#![warn(clippy::use_self)]
```

### B. `.clippy.toml` additions

```toml
allow-unwrap-in-tests = true
allow-expect-in-tests = true
cognitive-complexity-threshold = 20

disallowed-macros = [
    { path = "std::println",  reason = "library code must not print" },
    { path = "std::eprintln", reason = "library code must not print to stderr" },
    { path = "std::dbg",      reason = "debug macro must not ship in library code" },
]
```

### C. `packages/michi-node/src/lib.rs`

Upgrade the panic-related lints to `deny` (panics crash the Node process), skip pedantic (the `i32 as usize` casts are intentional at the boundary):

```rust
#![deny(clippy::all)]
#![deny(clippy::unwrap_used)]
#![deny(clippy::expect_used)]
#![deny(clippy::panic)]
#![deny(clippy::indexing_slicing)]
#![warn(clippy::use_self)]
#![warn(clippy::string_to_string)]
```

### D. oxlint for the JS test file

`pnpm add -D oxlint` + `"lint": "oxlint --env node __test__/"` in `package.json` + a `lint-js` CI job. No config file needed beyond that.

